# Manifest of the wave-73 checks that ./run_all.sh reruns (section 6), read by run_wave73.sh.
#
# One block per check. Keywords, one per line:
#   check ID                  a short unique name
#   after ID[,ID]             start only once these checks have finished: a check that reads what an earlier check
#                             wrote (all-t reads even-second's values.json) names it here.
#   threads N                 slots the check holds when JOBS > 1, and the BLAS threads it gets (default 1). The dense
#                             linear-algebra checks are 4 to 6 times slower on one thread than on several, so they say 2.
#   slow                      not part of the default run (kept out for time); SLOW_CHECKS=1 runs it. Its expected result
#                             is still written here, and was reproduced when the manifest was made.
#   run DIR/CWD ARGS...       working directory under record/wave73, then the arguments to `python3 -B`.
#                             {OUT} is a per-check temporary directory for JSON output; nothing is written
#                             into the repository (the whole of record/wave73 is copied to a temporary directory first).
#   rc N                      expected exit code (default 0). Several scripts exit 1 BY DESIGN: one pre-registered line
#                             failed and the folder's REPORT.md says which. They are listed with rc 1 and that exact line.
#   need REGEX                a whole output line, as an extended regular expression, that must appear.
#   count LABEL N REGEX [ ::: EXCLUDE]
#                             exactly N lines must match REGEX (and not EXCLUDE). LABEL is `checks` or `plants`;
#                             the totals are what the README quotes.
#   same FILE                 the output must be identical to this stored file (path relative to record/wave73). Used for
#                             the analyses of stored raw lattice rows: they must reproduce the committed result files.
#   contains FILE             every line of this stored file must be reproduced, in order; the script may print more
#   skip DIR[/SCRIPT] REASON  a folder or script that is not rerun, and why. Every folder under record/wave73 must be
#                             checked or named here; the runner fails on a new folder nobody decided about.
#
# Any output line that mentions FAIL, FAILED, MISSED, MISMATCH, Traceback or Error is a failure unless one of the
# check's own `need` regexes matches it. A by-design failure is therefore pinned exactly: a second failing line, or the
# known one turning green, makes the run red.

# Checks are listed longest first; the runner starts them in this order, as many as the slots allow.

check charge-ref-area
run charge-ref scripts/ref_area.py {OUT}/area_formula.json
slow
need ^SUMMARY pass 8 fail 0 time [0-9.]+s$
count checks 8 ^PASS[ ]

