# ---- not rerun, and why ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
skip phys-id no script: a note on the identification of the charge, nothing to run
skip referee no script: the referee report on the assembled statement
skip std-theorems no script: the list of standard theorems used and the conditions of their use
skip even-blind/erun.py the scripts that compute new lattice rows or controls (erun*.py, evalidate*.py, validate.py, ectrl.py, ctrl_odd_compare.py): the report puts the whole campaign at hours and several GB; the analysis of the stored rows (eanalyze.py) is rerun
skip hinge-blind/run.py the scripts that compute new lattice rows or controls (run.py, validate.py, far_region.py, planar_check.py, control_double.py, dev_*.py): the report gives about 75 minutes and 6 GB for the campaign; the analyses of the stored rows (analyze.py, controls.py, addendum_rule.py, predict_check.py) are rerun
skip even-proof/scripts/even_lemma_a.py about 3.5 minutes, and exits 1 by design (C2 and C3, as its report says); its extension even_lemma_a_ext.py is in the manifest, marked slow (190 s on every core, 400 s on two)
skip ruler-l/scripts/ruler_l.py l = 3 to 6 take 5 to 13 minutes each, and the plant run is not rerun; part 2 (the identity for every l) is rerun
skip ruler/scripts/ruler.py the --plant w3 run is not rerun; the main run is in the manifest, marked slow (77 s)
skip ruler-why/scripts/why.py the --plant k1 run is not rerun; the main run is in the manifest
skip odd-second/scripts/sup_cover.py about 3.5 minutes; its stored output is compared with the fresh primary values by odd-second-compare
skip ss-second/scripts/s3_limit.py about 5 minutes with the report's arguments (8001 0.04,0.02,0.01,0.005); with the script's own default arguments (a coarser grid) it ends S3 FAIL, which the report does not claim, so a rerun needs the report's arguments
skip even-tower/scripts/shale_check.py reads ../../hinge-e/out/e3_hyperbolic.json, a folder of the earlier record that is not published here
skip even-second/scripts/run_all.ps1 a Windows PowerShell wrapper with a venv path; the same two scripts are run directly
skip even-passage/scripts/scan_constants.py exploration only, prints no verdict
skip beyond-ref/scripts/beyond_ref.py about 13 minutes (795 s in its second registered run against a ten-minute fence), and both registered runs exit 1 by the report's own account (one of the referee's thresholds was set wrong); there is no passing run to pin
skip primary-sources no script: the list of primary sources that were read
